{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792923417,"nonce":"PWmH6yOBb8rHOJhY0sWy4qmh+o8=","title":"A Python module's body does not run again on reload","message":"Loading a Zyntax module whose language has an entry (Python's module statements) compiles it and runs the body. Reloading it took the function-swap path (reload_typed_program), republished and fired the before-notice, but never ran the body again, so a module-level registration (ChimpMonk's guests example: WorldTime.scene.addSystem(...) at top level of game/pulse.py) was removed by the reload notice and not made again. Lua reloads through run_module, which runs the chunk, and Wren re-runs its module. Fix: after the swap and the notice, run the entry again, as an import (and Python's importlib.reload) does. Reported by the ChimpMonk session.","files":null}]}